Progress.

46
00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.677
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:38.517 --> 00:02:41.236
Visal, why should countries work together?

48
00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:46.021
International cooperation leads to global progress.

49
00:02:47.117 --> 00:02:48.338
Give an example.

50
00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:54.503
The development of vaccines was faster because of global collaboration.

51
00:02:55.617 --> 00:02:56.989
Anything else?

52
00:02:58.083 --> 00:03:01.639
The protection of the oceans needs a united effort.

53
00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.463
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:08.129
Grammar focus: Nominalization.

55
00:03:08.429 --> 00:03:09.743
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:13.808
International cooperation leads to global progress.

57
00:03:14.717 --> 00:03:17.808
The development of vaccines was faster thanks to teamwork.

58
00:03:18.717 --> 00:03:21.610
The protection of the oceans needs a united effort.

59
00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:31.326
Nominalization turns verbs into nouns: cooperate → cooperation, protect → protection. It makes your English sound formal.

60
00:03:32.083 --> 00:03:36.454
Be careful! Don't say: International cooperate leads to progress.

61
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.979
Say: International cooperation leads to progress.

62
00:03:42.279 --> 00:03:45.567
Use the noun: cooperate → cooperation.

63
00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:48.822
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:49.633 --> 00:03:50.960
Better Together.

65
00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.433
Big problems cross every border.

66
00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:58.290
International cooperation leads to global progress.

67
00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.542
The development of vaccines showed the power of partnership.

68
00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:06.404
Diplomacy helps countries reach a shared goal.

69
00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.713
A united effort can change the world.

70
00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.813
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.824
International blank leads to progress.

72
00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:22.021
A, cooperation. B, cooperate. C, cooperative.

73
00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:27.996
The answer is A: cooperation.

74
00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.916
Managing relations between countries is blank.

75
00:04:32.216 --> 00:04:36.682
A, diplomacy. B, partnership. C, progress.

76
00:04:40.233 --> 00:04:42.628
The answer is A: diplomacy.

77
00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.504
Between countries means blank.

78
00:04:45.804 --> 00:04:49.492
A, cross-border. B, united. C, shared.

79
00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:55.497
The answer is A: cross-border.

80
00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.538
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:05:00.383 --> 00:05:04.287
What global challenge do you think requires international cooperation?

82
00:05:13.083 --> 00:05:14.537
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:14.837 --> 00:05:24.409
Climate change requires international cooperation. The reduction of pollution in one country is not enough, so every country must work together.

84
00:05:24.709 --> 00:05:26.291
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:27.183 --> 00:05:31.287
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and nominalization.

86
00:05:31.587 --> 00:05:36.550
Today's value is global unity. When the world works together, we all go further.

87
00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:39.653
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

88
00:05:39.953 --> 00:05:44.080
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

